From: ADIOS scheduler analysis
Subject: [PATCH] adios: v3.3.2-SAGA -- implements 3 of the 4 previously
 deferred ChatGPT-review items

Applies ON TOP of adios-android14-6.1-v3.2.0.patch. Same base as
v3.3.1-SAGA. Previous revision deferred 4 valid-but-lower-priority
items from the ChatGPT code review; this implements 3 of them (the
4th, struct reorganization, remains deferred -- pure maintainability,
zero behavioral effect, still not worth the diff size right now).

1. force_shrink_model() moved off the completion hot path. Was called
   directly from adios_completed_request() (allocates via kmemdup
   under a spinlock, GFP_ATOMIC) after detecting sustained
   misprediction -- real work on the exact path this series has been
   trying to keep fast, at exactly the moment the device may already
   be under pressure. Now: completion just sets a per-model
   shrink_pending flag; the existing update_timer (already guaranteed
   to fire within 100ms of any completion via the pre-existing
   timer_reduce() call) drains the flag and does the actual shrink in
   its own context.

2. READ_ONCE/WRITE_ONCE added for sysfs-tunable fields read on hot
   paths (lm_confidence_samples, lm_adapt_good_ratio_pct/
   lm_adapt_bad_ratio_pct, lm_interactive_idle_ms,
   lm_interactive_boost_ns, read_priority/dl_prio). Applied at the
   macro level (SYSFS_ULL_DECL, SYSFS_INT_DECL,
   SYSFS_INT_DECL_PAIRED) so it covers every tunable using those
   generators, not just the 5 identified as hot-path -- harmless
   where it's not strictly needed, correct where it is. Aligned u32/
   u64 don't tear on ARM64 in practice, so this doesn't fix an
   observed bug, but it's the technically correct way to publish
   sysfs-configurable state to a concurrent reader and would silence
   KCSAN if ever run under it.

3. Interactive-boost table doubled 16 -> 32 slots. Real Android easily
   exceeds 16 concurrently-relevant TGIDs (zygote, system_server,
   surfaceflinger, launcher, foreground app, GMS, media, vendor
   services...); at 16 slots, eviction is frequent enough that an
   evicted task's next read looks like "first sight" and gets
   re-boosted, undermining the "genuine idle-then-active" signal the
   mechanism is meant to capture. Still a fixed-size linear scan under
   a trylock (task_was_idle_and_gets_boost is unchanged otherwise) --
   a hash+probing redesign would scale further but remains deferred as
   more invasive than this fix is urgent.

STILL DEFERRED: struct reorganization (nesting the adaptive-controller/
interactive-boost fields into their own sub-structs instead of flat in
adios_data) -- zero behavioral effect, pure maintainability, skipped.

NOT submitted upstream. NOT compiled/tested against a real
android14-6.1 tree yet -- verified only for brace/paren balance and
that sizeof(iactv_table) auto-adjusts to the new slot count (it does,
no hardcoded 16 remained anywhere).
---
